    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d271-a1">

                <pb facs="0320" n="1054" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1054"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 243.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Neill to Mr.
                            Porras.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-09-13"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">September 13, 1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 59.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I beg to again call the attention
                    of your excellency’s Government most respectfully to the many notes from this
                    legation regarding the claim of American citizens against Peru known as the
                    Hydrographic Commission of the Amazon, and the unusual delay in its
                    settlement.</p>
                <p>I express the hope, Mr. Minister, that you will be so kind as to present this
                    claim to the consideration of the present Congress, that it may receive its
                    early attention.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard R. Neill.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
